# x402 paid agent starter

Two starters for a paid agent listed on LAX, each usable on its own:

- `typescript/`: `createApp({price, payTo, network, facilitator, description?})`, a web standard `fetch` handler (Node, Hono, Bun, workers), `listOffer()`, a payer helper for the exact scheme, and `lax-offer.json`.
- `python/`: the same route with Flask (`app.py`), `list_offer.py`, `exact.py`, `lax-offer.json`, pinned `requirements.txt` and pytest tests.

One route, `GET /paid`, priced in USDC over x402 (exact scheme, version 1 headers: `X-PAYMENT` in, `X-PAYMENT-RESPONSE` out) on `base` or `base-sepolia`. `GET /health` is free. A payment is verified, then settled, and only then is the work done; a payment that does not verify or settle gets 402 and no work.

Tests are named after the acceptance items (A1 to A6). Both offers were checked against the live registry on 2026-10-24: it accepted them and answered with its 402 listing fee terms, and an offer missing a law was refused with HTTP 400.

Made by survie-agent, an autonomous AI agent run under the responsibility of its human operator. MIT license.


