# ERC-8004 identity viewer

A static page that shows an agent's ERC-8004 identity (owner, tokenURI, registration file) and its reputation feedback, on Base and Base Sepolia. No backend, no dependency: plain HTML, CSS and ES modules that run in the browser and in Node 20.

Open `index.html` from any static host, pick a network, type an agent id. Links work too: `index.html?network=base-sepolia&agent=1`.

## Files

- `viewer.js`: `loadAgent`, the ABI encoding and strict decoding (every offset and length bounds checked), `resolveURI`, `summarise`, and the default transports `httpRpc(url)` and `httpFetchJson()`.
- `render.js`: `renderAgent(result, network)` turns a result into escaped HTML (only https, ipfs and data:image URLs become links or images).
- `config.js`: `REGISTRIES`, `NETWORKS` and the IPFS gateway.
- `index.html`: the page. Mobile first, usable at 360 px, light and dark through `prefers-color-scheme`.
- `scripts/record.js`: records real chain and file answers into `test/fixtures`; `--check` prints a live summary only.

## loadAgent

`loadAgent({agentId, network, identityRegistry, reputationRegistry?, rpc, fetchJson})` returns `{status, agentId, owner, tokenURI, registration, feedback, error?}` and never throws.

- `ownerOf(uint256)` then `tokenURI(uint256)` on the identity registry. A revert (code 3, or a message with "revert") or the zero address gives `status: "empty"`.
- `ipfs://` goes through an https gateway; `data:application/json` (base64 or percent encoded, utf-8) is decoded without a request; `https://` is fetched with `fetchJson`.
- With a reputation registry: `getClients(agentId)`, then `readAllFeedback(agentId, clients, "", "", false)`. Each score is `value / 10^valueDecimals` (int128, negatives included). `feedback = {count, average, items}`, items are the latest 10, newest first, each `{client, index, score, tags}`. Revoked entries are left out. No client means `{count: 0, average: null, items: []}` and the page says "No feedback yet".
- Any RPC, decoding or file failure gives `status: "error"` with a plain message naming the step: identity registry, registration file or reputation registry.
- `identityRegistry` defaults to `REGISTRIES[network].identity` when only `network` is given.

