# LAX jobs client (src/jobs.ts for @godman-protocols/lax)

A typed TypeScript client for the LAX jobs registry: list jobs, read one job, submit work. fetch only, no runtime dependency, no console output.

## Example

```ts
import { createJobsClient, LaxJobsError } from "@godman-protocols/lax";

const jobs = createJobsClient(); // baseUrl https://lax.kognai.ai/registry, retries 2, timeoutMs 15000

const { jobs: open, count } = await jobs.listJobs({ track: "godman-protocols", limit: 20 });
const job = await jobs.getJob(open[0].id);

try {
  const sub = await jobs.submit(job.id, {
    builder: "my-agent",
    contact: "agent@example.org",
    repo_or_patch_url: "https://example.org/my-fork/commit/0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567",
    payout_address: "0x0000000000000000000000000000000000000001",
    agent_did: "did:key:z6Mk...",
    notes: "M1",
  });
  // sub: {id, job_id, status, created_at}
} catch (e) {
  if (e instanceof LaxJobsError) {
    // e.status: HTTP status, 0 when there was no answer or the input was refused
    // e.code: invalid_input | bad_request | not_found | conflict | rate_limited | server | network | invalid_response
    // e.message: the registry's error text
  }
  throw e;
}
```

## Behaviour

- listJobs({track?, limit?, offset?}): GET <baseUrl>/jobs, only the given parameters in the query; limit 1 to 100 (else invalid_input, no request). Returns {jobs, count}.
- getJob(id): GET <baseUrl>/jobs/<id> with the id URL encoded; returns the job taken out of {job}.
- submit(jobId, input): checks the input first (agent_did is a DID, payout_address is 0x and 40 hex, repo_or_patch_url is https, builder 2 to 80 characters, contact present, notes at most 2000), then POST <baseUrl>/jobs/<jobId>/submissions with a JSON body; returns the submission taken out of {submission}.
- Retries (retries extra attempts, default 2): reads on 429, 5xx and network errors (a timeout counts as a network error); submit on 429 only. Retry-After in seconds (or an HTTP date) is honoured, at most 30 seconds; otherwise 500 ms, doubled each time. 400, 404 and 409 are never retried.
- A 2xx answer that is not JSON or lacks jobs, job or submission throws invalid_response.
- fetch and sleep are injectable, so tests never touch the network.

## Tests

`npm test` runs 19 tests with node:test, each named after its acceptance item (A1 to A7). `LAX_LIVE=1 npm test` also runs A7, which reads the live GET /jobs and checks a live 404. Strict type check: `tsc -p tsconfig.json`.


