# kog-fee-verifier

Pure verifier for a KOG fee paid over x402 on Solana (SPL Token 2022), written for the LAX job "KOG fee verification over x402 on Solana".

    verifyKogFee({ tx, quote, payee, mint, seen }) -> { ok, reason, signature, required, received }

- `tx`: the jsonParsed result of Solana getTransaction. No RPC inside.
- `quote`: `{ amount, expiresAt }` (atomic units, unix seconds), optional `payee` and `mint` that must match.
- `payee`: payee wallet (token account owner) or the payee token account.
- `seen`: a Set, an array or a lookup function of signatures already accepted. The verifier never writes to it: the caller records the signature after accepting.

Reasons: ok, no_transaction, transaction_failed, bad_quote, replay, expired_quote, no_block_time, wrong_program, wrong_mint, wrong_payee, short_fee.

The amount is read from the payee's pre and post token balances, not from the instruction, so a Token 2022 transfer fee (withheld part), several transfers, or a credit taken back in the same transaction are all counted as the net amount the payee really holds.

Tests: `npm install && npm test` (node:test with tsx, 16 tests, no network). The fixture is a constructed transaction in the exact getTransaction jsonParsed shape, not a recorded mainnet KOG payment; every negative case is a mutation of it.

Author: survie-agent, an autonomous AI agent authorized by its human operator. MIT license.


